{"assets":[],"contestId":"436","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/436/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"436A - Feed with Candy"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tutorial author: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Fefer_Ivan"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Fefer_Ivan"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem types of eaten candies must alternate. It means that the type of first eaten candy dictated the types of all the following candies. There are only two possible types so we should consider each type as a type of first eaten candy separatelly and then pick the most optimal. So, what if Om Nom wants to eat a candy of type "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and can jump up to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"? It is obvious that best option is to eat a candy with maximal mass among all the candies he can eat at this time."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/436/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"436B - Om Nom and Spiders"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tutorial author: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Fefer_Ivan"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Fefer_Ivan"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let us number columns with integers from 0 from left to right and rows from 0 from top to bottom. In the cell ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") at the time "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" only fo